1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,360
I'm Hieu. I build alone, and my background

2
00:00:03,360 --> 00:00:05,360
is not Solidity. It's QA.

3
00:00:05,360 --> 00:00:08,880
Eight years testing other people's software,

4
00:00:08,880 --> 00:00:12,000
finding the case nobody thought to try.

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:21,802
In June I found a real bug

6
00:00:21,802 --> 00:00:23,743
in Circle's CCTP sample app.

7
00:00:23,743 --> 00:00:26,307
I reported it. Circle shipped the fix

8
00:00:26,307 --> 00:00:27,554
twenty days later.

9
00:00:27,554 --> 00:00:29,356
Nobody did anything wrong.

10
00:00:29,356 --> 00:00:31,713
That was just waiting for a human.

11
00:00:31,713 --> 00:00:34,000
Proof of Break removes that wait.

12
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:38,170
Nine bounties live on Arc Testnet.

13
00:00:38,170 --> 00:00:39,255
Eighty-two tests.

14
00:00:39,255 --> 00:00:41,170
An agent that scans the board,

15
00:00:41,170 --> 00:00:43,660
picks its own job, and has claimed four

16
00:00:43,660 --> 00:00:45,830
of them on four different targets,

17
00:00:45,830 --> 00:00:48,000
with nobody touching the keyboard.

18
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:50,218
What I want from the Accelerator

19
00:00:50,218 --> 00:00:53,198
is the one thing I cannot test my way into:

20
00:00:53,198 --> 00:00:55,832
a real protocol putting a real release

21
00:00:55,832 --> 00:00:57,426
candidate on the board.

22
00:00:57,426 --> 00:00:59,990
The mechanism works. It needs someone

23
00:00:59,990 --> 00:01:02,000
other than me to point it at.
